THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE

This licence covers the contents of this repository. It does not cover the
tools the chain invokes, each of which carries its own terms. Nothing here is a
derivative work of them: they are called as separate processes or imported as
declared dependencies, and no code from them is copied into this repository.

  KLayout          GPL-3.0-or-later   invoked as an external application to
                                      execute a foundry rule deck
  MEEP and MPB     GPL-2.0-or-later   invoked as external processes for the
                                      time-domain and band-structure solves
  gdsfactory       MIT
  femwell          GPL-3.0
  scikit-fem       BSD-3-Clause
  gmsh             GPL-2.0-or-later
  SAX              Apache-2.0
  KLayout Python   GPL-3.0-or-later   imported as the `klayout` module
  numpy, scipy     BSD-3-Clause
  matplotlib       PSF-based
  pydantic, typer  MIT

Two consequences follow and both are stated so that a user is not surprised.

The `klayout` Python module is imported directly rather than invoked, and it is
GPL-3.0-or-later. **A distributor combining this repository with that module
into a single distributed work should take advice on the resulting obligations.**
Using it locally, which is what this repository does, raises no such question.

The `fem` and `fdtd` extras pull GPL-licensed tools. They are optional, the
chain runs without them, and each reports its absence rather than failing.
